56":"7618449ab13f0704ab550d05a34e74159e9fed81ca53f8fa948956f40171cbe4"},{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/registry/json/ErrorEntryTemplate.java","sha256":"5f0f3249ea0243051bcd3218492364c303215f81d49163c754005c63eaa3a741"},{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/registry/json/ErrorResponseTemplate.java","sha256":"f9029b36b0c9c4bae5a0c9986ce8f6d4139a7232bf34b454d83917e6e3e84aa2"},{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/tar/TarExtractor.java","sha256":"6fab7d55060922dc943381c15867749916a71bd4f514acc2ccec2d777f5260f1"},{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/tar/TarStreamBuilder.java","sha256":"db7afd2e2342aa5b82cf02d5e1cad7e42af2d380786dc074720c9bdf48239615"}],"queries":[{"id":"repoqa-592579daa84d76844f77","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To create a retriever that consistently provides a specific set of credentials, which are already known, for authentication purposes.\n2. **Input**: A set of credentials and a description of the source of these credentials.\n3. **Output**: A retriever function that, when called, logs the source of the credentials and returns these credentials wrapped in an `Optional`.\n4. **Procedure**: The method defines a retriever function that logs where the credentials were obtained from and then returns the credentials encapsulated in an `Optional` object to indicate their presence.\n","group":"GoogleContainerTools/jib","split":"dev","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/frontend/CredentialRetrieverFactory.java","grade":2,"spans":[[134,139]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-affd6b31795fd264997f","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To determine if a given string matches the default image tag commonly used in Docker images.\n2. **Input**: A string representing an image tag.\n3. **Output**: A boolean value; `true` if the input string is the default image tag, otherwise `false`.\n4. **Procedure**: The function compares the input string with the predefined default tag value. If they match, it returns `true`; otherwise, it returns `false`.\n","group":"GoogleContainerTools/jib","split":"dev","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/api/ImageReference.java","grade":2,"spans":[[261,263]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-ba90c4419d4dbe50ebfb","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To initialize a cache storage system using a specified directory, ensuring the directory exists or creating it if it does not.\n2. **Input**: A path to the desired directory for cache storage.\n3. **Output**: An instance of a cache management class configured to use the specified directory.\n4. **Procedure**: The method checks if the directory exists at the provided path and creates it if it does not. If an error occurs during the directory creation, an exception specific to cache directory creation issues is thrown. Upon successful directory setup, a new instance of the cache management class is returned, linked to the newly ensured directory.\n","group":"GoogleContainerTools/jib","split":"dev","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/cache/Cache.java","grade":2,"spans":[[55,62]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-98cbf777842f21a9cfd0","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To retrieve a set of key-value pairs that represent environment variables configured for a container.\n2. **Input**: No explicit input parameters are required as it operates on the internal state of an object.\n3. **Output**: Returns an immutable map containing the environment variables, where each key-value pair represents a variable name and its value. If no environment variables are set, it may return null.\n4. **Procedure**: The method accesses the internal storage that holds the environment variables set during the configuration of the container. It ensures the returned map is immutable to prevent external modifications, maintaining the integrity of the configuration.\n","group":"GoogleContainerTools/jib","split":"dev","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/configuration/ContainerConfiguration.java","grade":2,"spans":[[385,388]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-9f9ac0257e83d5a81d99","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To validate that the platform configuration of a build context matches the platform details of a non-manifest list base image, and to ensure that only one platform is specified when the base image is not a manifest list.\n2. **Input**: The function takes a build context containing the configuration details of the build, and a container configuration template that includes the platform details of the base image.\n3. **Output**: There is no return value; however, it throws a specific exception if the platform configuration does not match the base image's platform or if multiple platforms are specified for a non-manifest list base image.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - The function first checks if the base image configuration is specified by a path or an image reference.\n   - It then retrieves the set of target platforms specified in the build context.\n   - If multiple platforms are specified, an exception is thrown indicating that the base image must be a manifest list to support multiple platforms.\n   - If only one platform is specified, it compares this platform with the platform of the base image from the container configuration.\n   - If there is a mismatch and the specified platform is not the default, an exception is thrown indicating the mismatch between the configured platform and the base image's platform.\n","group":"GoogleContainerTools/jib","split":"dev","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/builder/steps/PlatformChecker.java","grade":2,"spans":[[39,76]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-b1eb517f61f534bed082","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To update the configuration file name for a Docker manifest entry.\n2. **Input**: A string representing the new configuration file name.\n3. **Output**: None; the function modifies the state of the object.\n4. **Procedure**: The method takes a string input and assigns it to the configuration file name property of the Docker manifest entry object.\n","group":"GoogleContainerTools/jib","split":"dev","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/docker/json/DockerManifestEntryTemplate.java","grade":2,"spans":[[62,64]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-b7a1f0a91a80d7a02472","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to manage container images by loading them into the local container registry, saving them from the registry to a file, and retrieving detailed information about specific images.\n2. **Input**: It accepts commands and parameters such as the path to an image tarball, an image reference, and an output path for saving images.\n3. **Output**: Depending on the operation, it returns the result of the image load operation, saves the image to a specified path, or provides detailed JSON formatted information about an image.\n4. **Procedure**: The function constructs and executes commands related to container management using a process builder. It handles input and output streams to interact with the process, manages error handling by capturing standard error output, and utilizes listeners to track byte counts during operations.\n","group":"GoogleContainerTools/jib","split":"dev","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/docker/CliDockerClient.java","grade":2,"spans":[[257,259]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-2b7608c791419f8360d4","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to handle the uploading of prepared image layers to a specified registry. This is part of a larger process in managing Docker image layers, specifically ensuring that the necessary layers are available in the target registry for further operations.\n2. **Input**: The function takes a list of futures representing layers that have been prepared for upload, and a factory for creating progress dispatchers to monitor the upload process.\n3. **Output**: It returns a list of futures, each containing a descriptor of a blob, which represents the result of the upload process for each layer.\n4. **Procedure**: The function first converts the list of prepared layer futures into a list of callable tasks that handle the uploading of each layer. It then schedules these tasks for execution. Each task is responsible for uploading a layer to the registry and returning a descriptor that identifies the uploaded blob.\n","group":"GoogleContainerTools/jib","split":"dev","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/builder/steps/StepsRunner.java","grade":2,"spans":[[397,407]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-521a21c706aefa7eda60","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To retrieve the location of a tarball archive file used for container image storage.\n2. **Input**: None.\n3. **Output**: Returns the file system path to the tarball archive.\n4. **Procedure**: Simply accesses and returns the path stored in a private variable within the class instance.\n","group":"GoogleContainerTools/jib","split":"dev","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/api/TarImage.java","grade":2,"spans":[[77,79]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-2a8dc6060706f010fd60","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function checks if all layers of a specified base image are present in the cache and retrieves the image if they are.\n2. **Input**: The function takes a combination of an image manifest and a container configuration, along with a boolean indicating whether the image is part of a manifest list.\n3. **Output**: Returns an optional image object; the image is returned if all its layers are cached, otherwise, an empty optional is returned.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - The function first verifies that the manifest is not null.\n   - It checks if all layers specified in the manifest are present in the cache.\n   - If any layer is missing, it returns an empty optional.\n   - If the manifest is of an older version, it directly converts the manifest to an image.\n   - For newer versions, it also checks the container configuration and, if the image is not part of a manifest list, verifies the platform configuration.\n   - Finally, it converts the manifest and container configuration into an image object and returns it.\n","group":"GoogleContainerTools/jib","split":"dev","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"jib-core/src/main/java/com/google/cloud/tools/jib/builder/steps/PullBaseImageStep.java","grade":2,"spans":[[504,526]]}],"answerability":"answerable"}]}
